{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30153 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "Methyl Lucidenate Q appears to have a mechanistic link to SNB-78 through multiple pathways, all involving the SDR family member 9 and other enzymes. The core mechanism involves the inhibition of dehydrogenase/reductase enzymes, which are targeted by Methyl Lucidenate Q, leading to the activation of 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, a compound that ultimately targets SNB-78. This pathway is supported by a high final score, indicating a strong and consistent relationship across three distinct evidence paths. Additionally, another pathway links Methyl Lucidenate Q to a different enzyme, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is also targeted by Leosibirone B, further reinforcing the involvement of SNB-78 in the downstream effects of these enzymatic activities. The integration of these pathways suggests that Methyl Lucidenate Q may exert its effects through a series of enzymatic interactions that ultimately lead to the modulation of SNB-78, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
